MICROSERVICES

MICROSERVICES PRACTICAL PROJECT

Detailed Question Paper

Project Title: Online Learning Management System

Technology: Java, Spring Boot, Spring Cloud, Eureka Server, Eureka Client, OpenFeign, REST API and MySQL

Project Structure: 1 Eureka Server + 7 Business Microservices

Objective: Build a complete microservices application in which each business responsibility is separated into an independent service. All services must register with Eureka, and specified inter-service communication must use OpenFeign with Eureka Service Discovery.

Important: This is an implementation-oriented project question. The names, responsibilities and communication relationships are fixed below. The student is responsible for designing the classes, database tables, controllers, services, repositories, DTOs, Feign clients, configurations and exception handling

----------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Project Overview

An online learning platform must manage students, courses, instructors, enrollments, payments, assignments and results. Instead of one large monolithic application, divide the system into seven independent business microservices.

Each service owns its responsibility and business data. A service must obtain another service's information through REST/OpenFeign rather than directly accessing another service's database.

