2. Basic Terms Used in This Project

Microservices Architecture
The application is divided into small independent services; each service has a specific business responsibility and runs as a separate Spring Boot application.

Spring Boot
Used to create and run each independent microservice.

Spring Cloud
Provides distributed-system tools. In this project, Eureka is used for service discovery and OpenFeign for service-to-service calls.

Eureka Server
Central service registry where microservices register themselves and from which service locations can be discovered.

Eureka Client
Each business microservice acts as a Eureka Client and registers with eureka-server.

OpenFeign
A declarative HTTP client used by one microservice to call another using the target service name.

Service Discovery
The caller asks Eureka for an available instance instead of using a fixed host and port.

